  "summary": "Recent preprints move topological diagnostics from bulk spectra toward wavefunction zeros, overlap determinants and localizer operators.",
  "synthesis": "Three of the four preprints diagnose topological invariants through objects other than the bulk Hamiltonian spectrum: zeros of the occupied-subspace overlap determinant for relative Chern and Z2 invariants (arXiv:2611.25037), wavefunction zeros and vorticities enforced by crystalline symmetry and readable from band-dispersion shifts (arXiv:2611.25028), and spectral localizer operators unifying Z and Z2 invariants for hinge modes, Dirac nodes and valley boundary modes (arXiv:2611.26160). The shared novelty is the shift of the diagnostic object toward overlaps, zeros and localizers. arXiv:2611.19328 applies a related logic to dynamical quantum phase transitions, attributing boundary effects to edge modes of the non-Hermitian Loschmidt matrix rather than Hamiltonian topology. It concerns dynamics rather than ground-state band topology and is the least direct fit to the dominant thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
